{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "04HK", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'E", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-etale-local-etale}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:59160506af40118f4f46d0a6a1fc6175b1b9ac008c9e063304781381860415fa", "source_text": "<ACCENT_0001>tale local structure of <ACCENT_0002>tale morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d0a3756ce165d0a94bee8c9313962bd5c5d6c33caec5057f5ee126187220689b", "unit_id": "tag:04HK:title"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04HK", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-unramified-etale-local}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bade6f19d6a1607192e9b6d4bb8b3841ea670c47ed6c40d9a2f38f033fc15513", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is a bit silly, but perhaps helps form intuition about <ACCENT_0001>tale\nmorphisms. We simply copy over the results of\nSection <REF_0001>\nand change ``closed immersion'' into ``isomorphism''.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:39f5750a49a6f4f22f36424a57e98ce96200e2526add171e5c145f04ee099c7b", "unit_id": "tag:04HK:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04HK", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$x_1, \\ldots, x_n \\in X$", "MATH_0003": "$s$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$x_i$", "MATH_0007": "$(U, u) \\to (S, s)$", "MATH_0008": "$V_{i, j} \\subset X_U$", "MATH_0009": "$i = 1, \\ldots, n$", "MATH_0010": "$j = 1, \\ldots, m_i$", "MATH_0011": "$V_{i, j} \\to U$", "MATH_0012": "$u$", "MATH_0013": "$V_{i, j} \\cap V_{i', j'}$", "MATH_0014": "$i = i'$", "MATH_0015": "$j = j'$", "MATH_0016": "$(X_U)_u$", "MATH_0017": "$x_i$", "MATH_0018": "$V_{i, j}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-etale-etale-local}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:74b4c686576b78d7b5ec8d56a9268edbc0ba8b7ae38f9f0bb25e6336ea679190", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:21bb758dc5344b30bf62e70f6e3c58f31cc3866eb1fa3c0d5d641ba435120cab", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be points having the same image <MATH_0003> in <MATH_0004>.\nAssume <MATH_0005> is <ACCENT_0001>tale at each <MATH_0006>.\nThen there exists an <ACCENT_0002>tale neighbourhood <MATH_0007>\nand opens <MATH_0008>, <MATH_0009>, <MATH_0010>\nsuch that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0011> is an isomorphism,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0012> is not in the image of <MATH_0013> unless\n<MATH_0014> and <MATH_0015>, and\n<STRUCT_0004> any point of <MATH_0016> mapping to <MATH_0017> is in some <MATH_0018>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:711a1e11390ec1883707179ea10fb46c8959787eda202a6f33539c9409283bc2", "unit_id": "tag:04HL:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04HK", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$V_{i, j} \\to U$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$V_{i, j} \\to U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-unramified-etale-local}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{theorem-etale-radicial-open}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7a9838721387a9010858db9d36db26513210abd37f17c7226f741745e6b1a4d1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:258404ac452bc0366b7672ffa752aaa4dfee0a3e83508a1b68af840ccc37a27f", "source_text": "An <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism is unramified, hence we may apply\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nNow <MATH_0001> is a closed immersion and <ACCENT_0002>tale.\nHence it is an open immersion, for example by\nTheorem <REF_0002>.\nReplace <MATH_0002> by the intersection of the images of <MATH_0003>\nto get the lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5acc83759072b3ed6e7e057b8f757dcc7e7eb9105f0f05a15d55db5c28070123", "unit_id": "tag:04HL:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04HK", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$x_1, \\ldots, x_n \\in X$", "MATH_0003": "$s$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$x_i$", "MATH_0008": "$(U, u) \\to (S, s)$", "MATH_0009": "$$\nX_U =\nW \\amalg \\coprod\\nolimits_{i, j} V_{i, j}\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$V_{i, j} \\to U$", "MATH_0011": "$W_u$", "MATH_0012": "$x_i$", "MATH_0013": "$f^{-1}(\\{s\\}) = \\{x_1, \\ldots, x_n\\}$", "MATH_0014": "$W_u$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-etale-etale-local-technical}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:94a060032cdac13c6e90d24fd1fd2e83ed838725d28043f9d1b1396cd3b55f15", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:38240102e2044743665afc9731f2140698d05288f19523d1aae93f4854c4aa7c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be points having the same image <MATH_0003> in <MATH_0004>.\nAssume <MATH_0005> is separated and <MATH_0006> is <ACCENT_0001>tale at each <MATH_0007>.\nThen there exists an <ACCENT_0002>tale neighbourhood <MATH_0008>\nand a finite disjoint union decomposition\n<MATH_0009>\nof schemes such that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0010> is an isomorphism,\n<STRUCT_0003> the fibre <MATH_0011> contains no point mapping to any <MATH_0012>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nIn particular, if <MATH_0013>, then\nthe fibre <MATH_0014> is empty.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3d9d73309e983255d4adaa020d63e7504175a3be8387d88accdd97ff1d634b42", "unit_id": "tag:04HM:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04HK", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$V_{i, j} \\to U$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-unramified-etale-local-technical}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-etale-etale-local}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ee528a035f7c617b47ceafec324f5323b7e4f28000d77643f820dee138fae03d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c2eea2e902d5b49b49abc88cf06747d5bb33a67b087315d9589b655c358f39ce", "source_text": "An <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism is unramified, hence we may apply\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nAs in the proof of\nLemma <REF_0002>\nthe morphisms <MATH_0001> are open immersions and\nwe win after replacing <MATH_0002> by the intersection of their\nimages.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0783a1c9da2fe37c42f902fdbf8aa35e14128fe3299a90121b3e709cf704b685", "unit_id": "tag:04HM:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04HK", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5f14daefaddc86b6cce6d7b34e6ba5d05dd051631c2c59c48c7cb43a6cf12c5e", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following lemma is in some sense much weaker than the preceding one\nbut it may be useful to state it explicitly here. It says that a finite\n<ACCENT_0001>tale morphism is <ACCENT_0002>tale locally on the base a\n``topological covering space'', i.e., a finite product of copies of the base.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d79de8acebcfdbb3c8c733ec0246419efd5abcd6be1c20d7e370430849223b2a", "unit_id": "tag:04HK:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04HK", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$s \\in S$", "MATH_0003": "$(U, u) \\to (S, s)$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nX_U = \\coprod\\nolimits_j V_j\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$V_j \\to U$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-etale-etale-local}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:793dc679d6985963a68cba25addbf3572b4eb745ca39af1b1c4a29bd035e07d6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3b09333ee05c3953ab9d501fd0f986746037c16482fd1750417bc64051d36843", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a finite <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002>. There exists an <ACCENT_0002>tale neighbourhood <MATH_0003>\nand a finite disjoint union decomposition\n<MATH_0004>\nof schemes such that each <MATH_0005> is an isomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e564a4a9ab3583b27619e295d76afdf243bc5f3a8e11a1337a028d75d1c39350", "unit_id": "tag:04HN:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04HK", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$V_{i, j} \\to U$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-finite-unramified-etale-local}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-etale-etale-local}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ee528a035f7c617b47ceafec324f5323b7e4f28000d77643f820dee138fae03d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:02d65a1a9cea8dd7f373fcb78f971047943ed9680bb585b94fbe830a8076d191", "source_text": "An <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism is unramified, hence we may apply\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nAs in the proof of\nLemma <REF_0002>\nwe see that <MATH_0001> is an open immersion and we win\nafter replacing <MATH_0002> by the intersection of their images.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3ecfab7123ddb0b0ee4b2ff1e52df86ca6ad050c59c2d7c9d55d84fdab4a43c5", "unit_id": "tag:04HN:proof"}
